      <h2>Platform Coverage</h2>
      <p>Car Alpha provides data and guidance for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>213,000+ indexed pages</strong> covering vehicle makes, models, model years, and state-specific ownership guides</li>
        <li><strong>50+ vehicle manufacturers</strong> from mainstream brands to luxury and specialty marques</li>
        <li><strong>3,500+ model-year combinations</strong> with full NHTSA specification data</li>
        <li><strong>All 50 US states</strong> with insurance, lemon law, registration, and EV incentive coverage</li>
        <li><strong>Original editorial content</strong> covering VIN education, recall awareness, insurance guidance, and ownership best practices</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Technical Architecture</h2>
      <p>Car Alpha is built on a hybrid static and edge-rendered architecture. Core content pages are statically generated at build time for maximum performance. High-volume dynamic pages (vehicle + state combinations) are rendered at the edge via Netlify Edge Functions using precompiled data, with CDN caching for sub-second response times. The result is a platform that scales to handle millions of page views with no database dependency and no external API calls at request time for content pages.</p>
      <p>The VIN decoder and recall checker query NHTSA APIs client-side, ensuring real-time data accuracy. The VIN scanner runs entirely in the browser, with no server-side processing of camera data.</p>

